    </div>

    <div class="chapter reveal"><span class="bignum">01</span><div class="num">Chapter One</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="what">What a brand actually is — not colours and fonts</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">A brand is the consistent promise and feeling people associate with you — what you reliably deliver and how it makes them feel. Colours, fonts, and logos are how a brand is expressed, but they are not the brand itself.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Think of a brand you trust without thinking. You don't trust it because of its font. You trust it because it has kept the same promise every time you've encountered it. <strong>Consistency is the whole mechanism — a brand is just a promise repeated until people believe it.</strong> The visual layer only works once there's a promise for it to carry.</p>
    <div class="box tip reveal"><span class="tag"><span class="g">✦</span> The Edit</span><p>A quick gut-check: if you removed your logo from your content, would anyone still know it was yours? If yes, you have a brand — a voice, a point of view, a consistent feeling. If the logo is the only thing identifying you, the brand is still just decoration.</p></div>

    <div class="triptych offset reveal">
      <div class="photo mask img" style="background-image:url(/images/library/detail-shelf-styling-02.jpg);background-size:cover;background-position:center"></div>
