    <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
    <h3 class="reveal">What is branding for a small business?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Branding is the consistent promise and feeling people associate with your business — what you reliably deliver and how it makes them feel. The logo, colours, and fonts express that promise, but the promise itself, kept consistently, is the actual brand.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">Do I need a designer to build a brand?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">No. The hardest and most important part — defining your promise, your reader, and your voice — is thinking, not designing. The visual choices are a small, repeatable set you can make yourself with free tools once the promise underneath is clear.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">How can a faceless brand feel personal?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Through voice and consistency. A faceless brand feels personal when it has a clear point of view, a recognisable way of writing, and a promise it keeps every time — all the things a personality does, carried by the brand instead of a face.</p>

